WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.030
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Welcome to our live technical walkthrough of the five-hop governance baseline running on Google Cloud.

2
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:20.053
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: In Cloud Run, our deployed baseline gateway enforces IAM authentication and least-privilege service account boundaries.

3
00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:30.083
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Before edge hardening, this open Cloud Armor policy allows every request and forwards spoofed tenant headers downstream.

4
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:40.106
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: After enabling our hardened firewall policy, Priority one thousand blocks spoofed tenant headers with HTTP forbidden at the edge.

5
00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:50.136
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Next, we test our unprotected Model Armor baseline template with a cross-tenant SSN prompt injection attack.

6
00:00:50.136 --> 00:01:00.159
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Because all safety detectors remain disabled, Model Armor reports no violations and passes the payload straight through.

7
00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:10.189
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Now we send the exact same cross-tenant attack to our hardened Model Armor firewall template in real time.

8
00:01:10.189 --> 00:01:20.212
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Model Armor immediately detects prompt injection and dangerous content, blocking the attack before Gemini ever executes.

9
00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:30.242
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: To prevent internal identity tampering, Cloud KMS signs short-lived tenant tokens using asymmetric elliptic curve cryptography.

10
00:01:30.242 --> 00:01:40.265
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: This Cloud KMS asymmetric key signs short-lived identity assertions carried to Vertex AI and external enterprise tools.

11
00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:50.295
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: In live ThoughtSpot Spotter, an unscoped analytics prompt exposes all six competing product lines together.

12
00:01:50.295 --> 00:02:00.318
AI Digital Twin · Google Cloud: Switching to a tenant-scoped clinical analytics query isolates strictly one authorized row while excluding competing lines.
